        LastRefRuling=(RULED 2026-09-04 by Tony, R1. lastREF answers what was referenced LAST, calls included, and there is no bracket. A bare accessor read after an intervening call is the READER's problem and the spelling is CAPTURE, THEN CALL -- with := and not =, bear-trap #41. Bracketing it would make what was referenced last mean something else; the singleton is the design, not a defect. What capture-then-call CANNOT fix is the CALLEE's own bare reads, because there the wrong thing is the value passed rather than the timing: with shadowCensus's caller respelled, scDcol's bare datA still reads the cursor holder under the flip and marks every row, D going 23 to 84 while the M column agrees exactly at 13 on both arms. That residue is R2's and is recorded rather than re-pinned.#);
