            JitOpDot=(UNREACHED, and the one worth watching. Instruct.rtn:327 gates to jitEmitDot BEFORE the bare-accessor fixup at :331, so on the JIT road opDot never consults lastREF at all. jitEmitDot bakes argument as a constant address at emit time and carries NO jitDegrade, so a null left operand -- which is exactly the bare-accessor case -- is baked as a null rather than resolved or refused. Read, not measured: the rung that would measure it is not yet buildable, see LastRefAgreementRung.#);
