        ArgBindingSites=(THREE, and the third is the one a reader will not predict. All are gated on gNoUnwrap. GroupActions.runOP.argBinding is the main funnel and it covers BOTH ROADS AT ONCE, because runOP's operand fetch is upstream of jitSeedField and all five dispatch arms -- operator, method, rule, action, command -- take target and arg from there. ruleActions.aCTionIterate.argBinding restates it for an iterate source, ahead of the holds-a-pointer refusal, because iterate reads input[1]/input[2] directly and never passes through runOP. jitEmitters.jitEmitBareRead.argBinding restates it a THIRD time because PRINT ITEMS ARE SEEDED THERE, not through runOP -- without it a jitted `print argument` reads the holder's storage and prints an address at degrade count 0, which is that function's own 75102656 one road over.#);
