    GroupsExtMirror=(RULED 2026-09-05 by Tony. A groups.ext line is a ROUTING declaration, not a signature contract -- and knowing which it is changes what drift in it costs.#):
        MirrorWhatItDoes=(tok resolves an extern BY NAME. Tony's words: it does not worry about parameters, it finds jitInlinePop by name and is satisfied. What the line actually decides is WHICH `external <Header>.h` BLOCK the name sits in, and therefore which #include tok emits -- which is why relocating a declaration between blocks is a real change and why a block ADDITION has a blast radius past the files a stroke retok'd.#);
        MirrorWhatItIsNot=(The PARAMETER LIST IS DOCUMENTATION THAT NOTHING CHECKS. tok never reads it; the C++ compiler never sees it, because the whole .rtn chain is ONE translation unit with the real GroupRules.h prototype in scope. So a mirror can disagree with its own function's arity indefinitely and every build, canary and fleet row stays green.#);
        MirrorMeasured=(2026-09-05, and the measurement IS the proof rather than an illustration: correcting jitInlinePop's mirror from zero parameters to one and running a full bare tokall produced ZERO codegen change. Byte-identical .mm and .h. Nothing downstream had ever been reading it.#);
        MirrorDriftClass=(⚠ SILENT BY CONSTRUCTION, and it belongs to bear-trap #45's family -- a name that RESOLVES but MEANS LESS THAN IT READS. Two instances found by census on the day the rule was written: jitInlinePop (mirrored 0, real 1) and opDivEQ (mirrored 1, real 2, while its own siblings opPlusEQ and opMinusEQ were already correct). Both fixed. The extern canary read 350 across both, as it must -- it counts definitions in a translation unit and has no view of this at all.#);
        MirrorTheRow=(genLadder/pop.sh carries the census as a fleet row PINNED AT ZERO over 291 comparable names, compared by ARITY rather than by type text because the mirror writes `GroupItem` where the header writes `GroupItem *` and that difference is not drift. It has an anti-vacuity guard -- a comparable count below 250 fails as a broken census rather than passing as zero drift -- and its H7 negative control was run: one mirror broken on purpose reports `1 of 291 drift -- opDivEQ` and names the offender. ⚠ A ROW AND NOT A STANDALONE LINT, deliberately: the census is the lint, it costs nothing where it sits, and a separate script would be a second population for one subject.#);

